## Context
Child of tracker 1252 (forge-less raid, gaze and merge); design in 1252's `## Raid annotation (design, 2026-10-27)` and `## Advisor ruling (2026-10-27)`.
Interface per the advisor ruling point 3: resolve(ref) -> id, branch, base, head, state, mergeable, body,
close claims; comments; checks; comment; append_body_line with read-back; create, ready, auto_merge_armed,
disarm, merge, read_back (gh backend lifted from raid_land.GhForge). Backend chosen by `--forge auto|gh|none`
/ `IDH_FORGE`. On `none`: resolve from `branch:<name> [base=<ref>]` by git only; comments and checks empty;
comment, append_body_line, ready, disarm a typed no-op; auto_merge_armed False; merge and read_back raise a
typed refusal until C5 (a silent no-op merge would read back "merged" on nothing).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] scripts/forge.py exposes those operations with gh and none backends; no caller is moved.
- [ ] The adapter's tests run with `gh` absent from PATH and with a stub `gh`.
- [ ] The forge path is unchanged (its tests pass); the harness gate passes.

Related: [[1252]].
